The '''Lada Niva Legend''',<ref name=Ladapress>{{Cite web|title=LADA Niva Legend: the new name for the iconic model – Press-releases – News – Official website LADA|url=https://www.lada.ru/en/press-releases/118503.html|access-date=2021-01-17|website=LADA official website|archive-date=13 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210113112447/https://www.lada.ru/en/press-releases/118503.html|url-status=live}}</ref> formerly called the '''Lada Niva''', '''VAZ-2121''', '''VAZ-2131''', and '''Lada 4×4''' ({{langx|ru|link=no|ВАЗ-2121, ВАЗ-2131, Лада Нива}}), is a series of [[four-wheel drive]], small (hatchback), and compact (wagon and pickup) [[Off-road vehicle|off-road cars]] designed and produced by [[AvtoVAZ]] since 1977. Initially aimed at the rural market, later models also targeted urban users. The three- and later five-door 4×4 hatchbacks were sold under the [[Lada]] marque in many markets,<ref>https://www.lada.ru/en/ {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210802222700/https://www.lada.ru/en/ |date=2 August 2021 }} Push cars icon and scroll down</ref> and have been in continuous production since 1977.

In the 1990s, three- and five-door wagons on a {{convert|50|cm|in|0|abbr=on}} longer wheelbase and an extra-long wheelbase pick-up were added to the range.{{Clarify|reason=What does "range" mean here?|date=January 2022}} After the [[Land Rover series|original Land Rover]] and its successor, the [[Land Rover Defender]], were discontinued in 2016, the Niva became the longest-production-run off-road light vehicle still manufactured in its original form. By the end of 2020, an estimated 650,000 Lada Nivas had been sold globally.<ref name="Lada20-12">{{Cite web |title=AVTOVAZ has started production of the new LADA Niva Travel |type=Press Release |url=https://www.lada.ru/en/press-releases/118463.html |date=2020-12-21 |access-date=2021-01-17 |website=LADA official website |archive-date=21 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210121045737/https://www.lada.ru/en/press-releases/118463.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

The Lada Niva is the world's first mass-produced off-road vehicle with a [[unibody]] construction (fully integrated body and frame).<ref>Six years ahead of the 1983 (for the 1984 model year) American [[Jeep Cherokee (XJ)]].</ref> It is the predecessor of current [[crossover SUV]]s, most of which are built similarly.

In August 2020, Lada took over production of the 2003 [[Lada Niva II|Chevrolet Niva]] and rebranded it the "new" Lada Niva.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://info.avtovaz.ru/press-releases/117703.html |title=Niva возвращается в семью LADA! |trans-title=Niva returns to the Lada family |language=ru |access-date=16 August 2020 |archive-date=17 October 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201017140636/http://info.avtovaz.ru/press-releases/117703.html |url-status=live }}</ref> In December 2020, the new Niva was further rebranded as the '''Lada Niva Travel''', while the old model was renamed '''Lada Niva Legend''' in January 2021.<ref>{{Cite web |title=AVTOVAZ has started production of the new LADA Niva Travel – Press-releases – News – Official website LADA |url=https://www.lada.ru/en/press-releases/118463.html |access-date=2021-01-17 |website=LADA official website |archive-date=21 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210121045737/https://www.lada.ru/en/press-releases/118463.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="Ladapress" />


